# {{ project_name }}

Generated from the Paved CDK template.

## First time

```bash
uv sync          # pulls the platform library straight from GitHub (pinned tag)
uv run cdk synth # builds the template — deterministic, no AWS login needed
```

The platform library is declared as a git dependency in `pyproject.toml` (no extra
package registry needed). `uv sync` clones it at tag `{{ platform_version }}`.

## Deployment — three stages, one pipeline

Pushing to `main` runs the **central, shared pipeline** (maintained in
`{{ platform_repo }}`): lint → synth + cdk-nag → deploy **dev → test → prod**.
Every DS project runs the exact same pipeline; it updates when you `copier update`
(which bumps the `@{{ platform_version }}` ref in `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`).

One-time per repo: create GitHub Environments `dev`, `test`, `prod`, each with a
secret `AWS_DEPLOY_ROLE_ARN` (the OIDC deploy role of that account) and, for
`prod`, required reviewers. Your team's three accounts are provisioned for you.

## Pulling platform updates

```bash
copier update     # re-renders against the latest template, bumps the platform tag
```

## What you do NOT configure

VPC, subnets, KMS encryption, IAM permissions boundary, log retention and
governance tags are resolved automatically from whichever of your three accounts
the pipeline is deploying into. Just add platform constructs in `app.py`.
